ad of writing a long and complicated letter in the commission letter, it would be more effective and convincing to send a threatening letter. If he thought so\u2026\"\n[3928] \"So Yudu sent the threatening letter to you just to get you here.\" The detective seemed convinced. [3929] \"Yes. Yudu skillfully took advantage of my temperament. When the detective put his hand on Yudu's desk, the palm got sticky with the glue that Yudu spilled while pasting the threatening letter. That's a small piece of evidence.\" [3930] \"In short, all obstacles were cleared, and I was finally able to conclude that the murderer was Kiri.\" [3931] However, Mochizuki's appearance was just as he said, that of a loser. The attitude of being intoxicated with victory in past cases was gone. [3932] \"I had to retreat into the mountains just to reach this insignificant step, while she, in a foreign country where she stayed for only five months, alone, accomplished so much. She is the true genius\u2026\"\n[3933] Tsujimura, who had always disliked praise for the criminal, did not object at this time. [3934] \"Of course, maybe she is a god beyond everything.\" [3935] Mochizuki sighed and began to tell the story of the case itself. [3936] \"The concept of comparing a country's name to a crossword puzzle\u2026it's terrifying and imaginative. It can't be done without the right environment and characters. However, this mansion has everything. All the pieces, all the stage settings\u2026\"\n[3937] Mutsuzaki sat down on the bench, as if standing was a great burden. [3938] \"Let's start with the Ito-Hyoma murder case. Ito approached us with a request. As I mentioned earlier, Mochizuki had no part in it. Our involvement, although unexpected for her, might have been a beneficial stimulus. Thus, she slightly modified the script. Consequently, I found myself playing the role of an extra to enhance the drama's impact. [3939] \"However\u2026the so-called god\u2014let's call it that\u2014wasn't satisfied and led us into a chaotic maze with further pranks. That was the 'Hell Gate' room.\" [3940] \"A locked room\u2026\" The detective didn't refute Mutsuzaki's statement. [3941] \"Let me explain in order. Under the influence of Mukemizu's flattery, UMAYama quietly returned to his own house that day. [3942] \"It was around 3 am, and UMAYama, who knew nothing, was guided by Mukemizu to his room. At this point, Mukemizu struck UMAYama from behind with a blunt object. Although it was only one blow, it was very powerful, so UMAYama seemed to be dead. At least Mukemizu thought so. In fact, as later determined, he had only fainted and was not yet at the point of death. This is important, so please remember it. [3943] \"Mukemizu moved the unconscious UMAYama into It\u00f4's room. There was another body that Mukemizu thought she had killed in It\u00f4's room, but in fact It\u00f4 had only fainted. [3944] \"Mukemizu intended to carry out the execution according to the 'Lecchonawa Book', using the painting in Kanayan's house. Perhaps she saw herself as the reincarnation of God. This action was both sacred and demonic. This can be seen from the cruel method of execution. [3945] \"Mukemizu made the two sit down on the carpet side by side and simultaneously cut off their heads with a large knife. Now I even know the order in which they sat on the carpet. If Mukemizu had swung the large knife from the right, then facing them, it would have been It\u00f4 on the right and UMAYama on the left.\" [3946] \"Is this important?\" [3947] \"Yes.\" [3948] The Muketsumi nodded, his face devoid of a smile. [3949] \"Up to this point, everything was proceeding according to plan. Even if the method was extraordinary, if it was just a matter of killing someone, the situation would have matched the motive. [3950] \"However, at that very moment, the hand of the gods intervened. Perhaps it was a whim of heaven...\n[3951] I could sense Mukai's growing excitement. I was explaining, yet I was getting excited myself. We were all waiting for the next sentence. [3952] \"Mistuhide sliced off the heads of the two men horizontally. The sharp blade must have completed the task in an instant. An instant later, there should have been two heads and two bodies left. If everything went according to plan\u2026\"\n[3953] \"Do you know the key to 'Takatori'? Strike horizontally with a mallet to make the lowest or middle wooden wheel fly smoothly. But if you fail, due to gravity and friction, the upper wooden wheel will also fly out, causing the whole stack of blocks to collapse and the game to fail.\" [3954] \"Mistuhide made the same mistake. Don't you understand? Mistuhide swung down the sword, no, horizontally. Then\u2026 terrifyingly, when the sword passed through Itou's neck, Itou's head remained on the blade's surface.\" [3955] \"It happened in a mere zero point zero one second, so Mistuhide couldn't have noticed the anomaly. The blade, now carrying Itou's head, aimed at the neck of the man standing nearby, Haya, and cut off his head.\" [3956] \"It was at this moment that the head of the horse was knocked aside by the Ito's head brought by the blade. At the same time, under the action of Newton's third law of motion, Ito's head was pushed out of the blade in the opposite direction. Just a few millimeters below the blade, the cut surface of the horse's body was there, and Ito's head fell vertically and landed on the cut surface without deviation. [3957] \"...\n[3958] \"I have just said so much, but everything happened in the blink of an eye. It was probably less than a hundredth of a second. But because it was such a brief moment, a miracle happened. [3959] \"The time it took to cut off the head was too short, so Ito's brain cells did not die. To be precise, the brain cells and sensory nerves, as well as the neural fibers that form the conduction center, are still alive. And these neural fibers' fine mesh merged with the neural fibers in the horse's body. [3960] \"Impossible!\" [3961] 